\subsection{Early Warning Analysis}
\label{sec:early_warning}

We analyze within-generation temporal dynamics by measuring signal deviation from the clean baseline at intermediate training checkpoints ($3\%$--$100\%$ progress).

\paragraph{Signal deviation trajectories.}
Table~\ref{tab:early_warning} reports signal deviation at key checkpoints for the 100\% synthetic condition.
Stable rank diverges earliest ($18\pm4\%$ at step 50 / $3\%$ progress), while perplexity ratio provides the most reliable separation ($1.12\times$ at $3\%$ progress, growing to $33.6\times$ at completion).

